description.p:
The Bi-containing metal oxide deposited on the substrate may have the formula (Bi2θ2)2+(Am-ιBmθ3m+ι)2"I where A is Bi3+, L3+, L2+, Ca2+, Sr2+, Ba2+, Pb2+, or Na+, B is Fe3+, Al3+, Sc3+, Y3+, L3+, L4+, Ti4+, Nb5+, Ta5+, W6+, or Mo6+, and L is Ce4+, La3+, Pr3+, Ho3+, Eu2+, or Yb2+, and where 1 <m<5. The Bi-containing metal oxide may also have the formula B'^WOe; BiM03, where M is Fe or Mn; Ba2BiMθ6, where M is V, Nb or Ta; Pb2BiMOe, where M is V, Nb or Ta; 

Ba3Bi2M09, where M is Mo or W; Pb3Bi2M0g, where M is Mo or W; BaeBiMOis, where M is Mo or W; PbeBiMOis, where M is Mo or W; KBiTi2θe; or 

 These metal oxides can be obtained by decomposing precursors which contain the above-described metals.
